# Build context trimming. The core build needs source, cmake, deps and .git
# (for the revision header); it does not need 189MB of SQL, 24MB of runbook
# evidence, or any local build tree.
#
# Every pattern here is anchored at the context root -- `sql/` matches ./sql and
# nothing else. That mattered the moment the core moved into the core/
# submodule (ADR-0020): upstream's world data went with it, so the 130MB this
# file exists to keep out of the context came back as core/sql/ and had to be
# named again. The same trap waits for anything added below: check whether the
# core has one too.
runbooks/
sql/
core/sql/
docs/
core/docs/
patches/
ops/

# NOT ignored, and easy to add here by mistake: core/ itself, and .git. The
# builder stage does COPY . /src and configures the platform root, which
# FATAL_ERRORs if core/CMakeLists.txt is absent; and the revision header is
# produced by running git inside core/, which needs both core/.git (a file
# pointing into .git/modules/core) and .git itself.
**/build/
**/.vs/
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/CMakeFiles/
*.log

# ci.yml artefacts. The staged install (./stage) is deliberately NOT here - the
# ci-staged target COPYs it - but everything else the build job leaves behind is
# large and would only slow the context transfer down.
.ccache/
.sccache/
.vcpkg-cache/
.ci/
test-results/
image/
